%% DM26-0670

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant D as Domain actor
    participant F as Facade + Outbox
    participant Disk as Outbox file
    participant T as Transport
    participant B as Broker

    Note over F,B: Online. 41 and 42 were sent, only 41 acknowledged.
    T--xB: connection fails
    T-->>F: ConnectionLost
    F->>Disk: quiesce: write the unacknowledged entries (42) with their epoch and seq
    F->>F: state = Offline
    D->>F: Publish (43)
    F->>F: append to the outbox
    F->>Disk: append entry 43
    F->>T: respawn the transport, with backoff
    T->>B: connect and register (same registration id)
    alt the broker still has the session
        B-->>T: registered
    else the broker lost the session
        B-->>T: session mismatch
        T-->>F: SessionInvalidated
        T->>B: register fresh
        B-->>T: registered (new id)
    end
    T-->>F: Connected(registration id)
    F->>T: Subscribe for every remembered topic
    B->>B: the old connection is fenced: whatever it delivers late is ignored
    F->>T: retransmit the unacknowledged, in order: 42 then 43, same epoch and seq
    T->>B: PublishRequest 42, 43
    B->>B: 42 already accepted? acknowledge it again. 43 is new: accept it
    B-->>T: PublishRequestAck(42) and PublishRequestAck(43), each for its own message
    T-->>F: Acked(42), Acked(43)
    F->>F: outbox empty
    F->>Disk: remove the file
    F->>F: state = Online
    Note over B,T: If the broker restarted it also lost its record of 42, so it accepts 42 again.<br/>Subscribers drop that duplicate by the origin (publisher, epoch, seq) the message carries.
